<!--
  Exercise-challenge fixture. Unlike a Pre/Post bronchodilator session, an
  exercise challenge records a pre-exercise baseline plus one best curve per
  post-exercise time point, and Medikro does NOT prefix those later phases
  with "Post". They therefore all reach the baseline branch of the parser.

  Session 1 keeps the literal "Pre Phase" label on the baseline and labels
  the time points in Finnish. Session 2 labels every phase by time point
  with no "Pre Phase" anywhere, so only the timestamp ordering can identify
  the baseline. Both sessions put the HIGHEST FVC/FEV1 on the baseline and
  progressively lower values afterwards, which is what post-exercise
  bronchoconstriction looks like and is why the old last-row-wins behaviour
  under-reported baseline FVC.

  Phase labels and the TIME serial format below are taken from the real
  study exports: Pre/Post sessions run (Pre Phase, Post Phase), exercise
  sessions run (Baseline, Control, Chall02..Chall05, Recovery).
-->
